    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green. There's effectively one test class in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with a successful compile.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a derived field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year. I implemented it the same way the codebase already derives `displayName` and `initials` \u2014 as a computed value rather than a stored column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (after `customerCode`), so the OpenAPI generator produces the field + getter/setter on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   This zero-pads the two-digit year (e.g. year 2026 \u2192 `26`, 2005 \u2192 `05`), matching the test's `registrationDate` string `substring(2, 4)` derivation and yielding values like `SMI-0007-M26`.\n\nSince `customerCode` is generated and `registrationDate` defaults to the current date on create, every owner returned by the API now carries a correctly formatted `membershipNumber`.",
